1
00:00:00,959 --> 00:00:03,253
♪ <i>Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

2
00:00:03,336 --> 00:00:06,589
["Mr. Tailor" playing]

3
00:00:08,425 --> 00:00:10,468
- <i>♪ Fix it</i> ♪
- <i>♪ Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

4
00:00:10,552 --> 00:00:12,512
♪ <i>Holding the scissors</i> ♪

5
00:00:12,595 --> 00:00:16,141
♪ <i>One cut, and it's over</i> ♪

6
00:00:17,308 --> 00:00:18,852
[gunshots]

7
00:00:18,935 --> 00:00:19,853
[groans]

8
00:00:19,936 --> 00:00:21,146
[Samir, in English] <i>I was attacked.</i>

9
00:00:21,229 --> 00:00:22,313
[Artem, in English] <i>You were attacked?</i>

10
00:00:22,397 --> 00:00:23,481
[in English] Identities?

11
00:00:23,565 --> 00:00:25,108
[in English] Friends of Atoy.

12
00:00:25,191 --> 00:00:29,112
[Samir, in English] <i>We must find</i>
<i>his family, right now.</i>

13
00:00:29,195 --> 00:00:32,365
There were three men here, collecting.

14
00:00:32,449 --> 00:00:34,993
[Olga] <i>Those three men</i>
<i>you talked to, they're enemies!</i>

15
00:00:35,076 --> 00:00:36,119
[henchman 1] They're here.

16
00:00:36,202 --> 00:00:37,287
[Martina] <i>They're at Olga's house now,</i>

17
00:00:37,370 --> 00:00:39,873
<i>and hopefully by lunchtime,</i>
<i>we'll have Ibyang.</i>

18
00:00:39,956 --> 00:00:41,624
[in English] Finally, some good news.

19
00:00:42,250 --> 00:00:43,501
- [spritzing]
- [both screaming]

20
00:00:43,585 --> 00:00:44,878
- [screaming]
- [Olga] Ibyang! Come on, hurry!

21
00:00:44,961 --> 00:00:46,337
[Olga] Come on, come on! Hurry, hurry!

22
00:00:46,421 --> 00:00:48,923
[Samir, in English] <i>We need that woman</i>
<i>and her daughter!</i>

23
00:00:49,007 --> 00:00:50,759
[in English] Or that man will not talk!

24
00:00:50,842 --> 00:00:52,719
[in English] We can mimic
the woman's voice,

25
00:00:52,802 --> 00:00:54,137
and we can make her say anything we want.

26
00:00:54,220 --> 00:00:55,555
- [Olga shouts]
- [man grunts]

27
00:00:57,265 --> 00:00:58,808
- Ibyang! Come on.
- [groaning]

28
00:00:58,892 --> 00:01:00,185
No one make the wrong move!

29
00:01:00,268 --> 00:01:01,352
[Charmi] Move!

30
00:01:01,436 --> 00:01:02,854
Go there! Hurry!

31
00:01:02,937 --> 00:01:04,939
[Atoy, in English] <i>What--</i>
<i>What did you do to them?</i>

32
00:01:05,023 --> 00:01:05,982
[Samir, in English] <i>They are safe.</i>

33
00:01:06,066 --> 00:01:07,859
[in English] I will tell you
where the laptop is.

34
00:01:07,942 --> 00:01:09,402
[in English] You'd better
tell me the truth.

35
00:01:09,486 --> 00:01:11,571
[Audrey, in English] <i>I need</i>
<i>to talk to Atoy first.</i>

36
00:01:11,654 --> 00:01:14,324
Then together,
we'll tell Janine the truth.

37
00:01:14,407 --> 00:01:16,576
[Cita] <i>Olga, what happened?</i>

38
00:01:16,659 --> 00:01:18,620
<i>Why did Ame have to take the child away?</i>

39
00:01:18,703 --> 00:01:19,746
Is there a problem?

40
00:01:19,829 --> 00:01:22,999
[sighs] I've been calling Atoy
for a while now.

41
00:01:23,083 --> 00:01:25,460
My love, what are you going to tell Atoy?

42
00:01:25,543 --> 00:01:27,170
You can tell me.

43
00:01:27,796 --> 00:01:30,423
Atoy is Ibyang's real father.

44
00:01:31,591 --> 00:01:34,093
PREVIOUSLY

45
00:01:38,097 --> 00:01:39,808
[music fades]

46
00:01:41,935 --> 00:01:44,229
[Viktor, in English] Bring them all here.

47
00:01:45,104 --> 00:01:47,065
[in English] We will dismantle it…

48
00:01:48,149 --> 00:01:50,777
and we have men that can check the engines

49
00:01:50,860 --> 00:01:54,072
and parts to see
if we can salvage anything.

50
00:01:55,365 --> 00:01:59,911
[in English] If not, I have a machine
that can make it into scrap metal.

51
00:02:00,703 --> 00:02:02,122
[in English] You have a junkyard?

52
00:02:02,205 --> 00:02:03,331
[in Russian] Yes.

53
00:02:03,915 --> 00:02:06,501
[in English] In San Rodolfo, Bulacan.

54
00:02:06,584 --> 00:02:08,795
[Viktor, in English] Yes. I'm here now.

55
00:02:08,878 --> 00:02:11,673
[in English] But tomorrow, maybe not.

56
00:02:12,382 --> 00:02:14,134
[in English] Yes. Thank you.

57
00:02:16,136 --> 00:02:19,347
[tense music playing]

58
00:02:25,562 --> 00:02:27,021
[in English] So…

59
00:02:30,191 --> 00:02:35,989
[in English] You are the one
that attacked me in my office, huh?

60
00:02:36,072 --> 00:02:38,616
[music swells]

61
00:02:43,037 --> 00:02:45,081
[suave theme music playing]

62
00:03:05,101 --> 00:03:07,103
[music swells]

63
00:03:11,316 --> 00:03:12,901
[in English] What?!

64
00:03:14,193 --> 00:03:17,280
So, Atoy is Ibyang's real father?

65
00:03:17,363 --> 00:03:18,823
And you're her mother?

66
00:03:18,907 --> 00:03:19,782
So that means you're the parents?

67
00:03:19,866 --> 00:03:21,200
No, no, no, not like that.

68
00:03:21,284 --> 00:03:22,702
It's not like that.

69
00:03:22,785 --> 00:03:24,913
It's-- It's just Atoy who's the parent.

70
00:03:24,996 --> 00:03:25,955
What did you say?

71
00:03:26,039 --> 00:03:27,290
Aren't you the mother?

72
00:03:27,957 --> 00:03:29,417
[pensive music playing]

73
00:03:29,500 --> 00:03:31,419
I don't understand what you're saying.

74
00:03:32,337 --> 00:03:34,130
[Olga] Um…

75
00:03:35,548 --> 00:03:37,342
Don't be mad, huh.

76
00:03:38,384 --> 00:03:40,345
I'm not really

77
00:03:40,428 --> 00:03:41,971
Ibyang's real mother.

78
00:03:42,055 --> 00:03:43,932
[music fades]

79
00:03:44,015 --> 00:03:45,141
What?!

80
00:03:45,975 --> 00:03:47,685
[clears throat] So,

81
00:03:47,769 --> 00:03:49,187
you're a fake mother?

82
00:03:49,270 --> 00:03:50,980
Something like that, yes.

83
00:03:51,064 --> 00:03:52,774
- [suspicious music playing]
- [Olga sighs]

84
00:03:52,857 --> 00:03:56,486
I auditioned with Ma'am Martina
and Red Regalia. [inhales]

85
00:03:57,570 --> 00:04:00,573
They hired me
to pretend to be Ibyang's mother.

86
00:04:01,574 --> 00:04:05,245
The pay is quite big.

87
00:04:06,120 --> 00:04:07,538
I needed the money.

88
00:04:08,414 --> 00:04:09,499
That's terrible.

89
00:04:09,582 --> 00:04:11,751
How could you bear to deceive the child?!

90
00:04:11,834 --> 00:04:13,211
Don't you have a conscience?!

91
00:04:14,879 --> 00:04:16,756
[in English] I can't believe this.

92
00:04:16,839 --> 00:04:18,299
[in English] You're only beautiful
on the outside,

93
00:04:18,383 --> 00:04:20,593
but you're very ugly inside!

94
00:04:20,677 --> 00:04:22,720
[in English] How could you do this to me?

95
00:04:22,804 --> 00:04:24,430
[Emerson] Huh?

96
00:04:24,514 --> 00:04:25,890
So that means you're Red's employee!

97
00:04:25,974 --> 00:04:28,017
- You're Red's minion!
- [Olga] No!

98
00:04:28,101 --> 00:04:30,311
No, no. It's not like that-- [sighs]

99
00:04:30,395 --> 00:04:31,521
[sighs] I'm sorry.

100
00:04:31,604 --> 00:04:32,605
[Cita scoffs]

101
00:04:32,689 --> 00:04:34,357
It's just work.

102
00:04:34,440 --> 00:04:37,110
That's all it is.
It's just my job, promise.

103
00:04:37,193 --> 00:04:38,736
[Olga] Nothing else.

104
00:04:39,320 --> 00:04:40,613
That's why I'm here,

105
00:04:41,322 --> 00:04:46,035
because I found out
that Atoy is the real father of Ibyang,

106
00:04:46,619 --> 00:04:49,289
and Madam Martina plans to take her away.

107
00:04:49,372 --> 00:04:52,000
And how are we supposed to believe you?

108
00:04:52,083 --> 00:04:55,295
For all we know, you and the Regalias
have another plan!

109
00:04:55,920 --> 00:04:59,257
I can't take that thought
out of your mind. I'm sorry.

110
00:05:00,341 --> 00:05:03,303
But I'm here to set things right.

111
00:05:04,512 --> 00:05:06,472
You know, honestly,

112
00:05:06,556 --> 00:05:08,516
I even wanted to adopt the child.

113
00:05:10,893 --> 00:05:12,854
Because Ibyang has become dear to me.

114
00:05:14,063 --> 00:05:18,359
But then I found out that Atoy
is actually Ibyang's real father.

115
00:05:18,443 --> 00:05:20,028
That's why I'm here now.

116
00:05:20,695 --> 00:05:22,155
So, what now?

117
00:05:22,947 --> 00:05:24,490
Atoy isn't here.

118
00:05:24,574 --> 00:05:26,242
Actually, Atoy is missing.

119
00:05:27,243 --> 00:05:28,995
If Atoy isn't here,

120
00:05:29,078 --> 00:05:31,539
maybe don't tell anyone yet.

121
00:05:31,622 --> 00:05:33,708
Let's keep it between us for now.

122
00:05:34,208 --> 00:05:36,044
[tense music playing]

123
00:05:41,632 --> 00:05:42,967
[music fades]

124
00:05:43,051 --> 00:05:44,343
[grunts]

125
00:05:46,095 --> 00:05:46,971
- [groans]
- [in English] That's

126
00:05:47,055 --> 00:05:50,141
for attacking me in my office.

127
00:05:50,224 --> 00:05:51,893
- [pensive music playing]
- [Atoy inhales]

128
00:05:51,976 --> 00:05:53,978
[in English] But I must admit.

129
00:05:55,104 --> 00:05:57,857
[in English] I am impressed.

130
00:05:58,441 --> 00:06:04,739
[in English] You single-handedly
infiltrated the embassy.

131
00:06:04,822 --> 00:06:06,365
[cackles]

132
00:06:06,449 --> 00:06:08,201
Bravo!

133
00:06:08,910 --> 00:06:10,453
[pensive continues playing]

134
00:06:10,536 --> 00:06:14,957
[in English] But did you think
you could get away with this?

135
00:06:16,834 --> 00:06:22,465
[in English] If you don't want anything
to happen to the woman and child,

136
00:06:24,092 --> 00:06:26,969
you will tell me!

137
00:06:27,053 --> 00:06:29,055
[in English] Where is the laptop?!

138
00:06:31,599 --> 00:06:33,976
[in English] Do you want to know
where the laptop is?

139
00:06:35,812 --> 00:06:38,064
[in English] I need proof of life first.

140
00:06:42,819 --> 00:06:45,238
[in English] You want proof of life?

141
00:06:48,699 --> 00:06:50,034
Hmm?

142
00:06:51,744 --> 00:06:54,205
[in English] How about I just take yours?

143
00:06:55,248 --> 00:06:56,415
Hmm?

144
00:06:58,000 --> 00:06:58,960
‪[grunts]

145
00:06:59,043 --> 00:07:01,796
[grunting and groaning]

146
00:07:02,463 --> 00:07:04,006
[grunts]

147
00:07:08,177 --> 00:07:10,012
[Lily sobs]

148
00:07:10,721 --> 00:07:13,182
[Lily, in English] Sir, please.
Stop. Stop. Stop, sir!

149
00:07:13,266 --> 00:07:15,143
[Lily, in English] Sir, please have mercy.

150
00:07:15,226 --> 00:07:16,727
[groans]

151
00:07:16,811 --> 00:07:19,021
[Viktor, in English] How dare you

152
00:07:19,105 --> 00:07:20,982
talk to me, traitor!

153
00:07:21,065 --> 00:07:23,443
[in English] No, no, no, no!
Stop! Stop, stop, stop!

154
00:07:23,526 --> 00:07:25,445
[in English] No, no, no. Don't hurt her!

155
00:07:26,028 --> 00:07:27,405
[Atoy, in English] I will stop.
I will stop.

156
00:07:29,782 --> 00:07:31,909
[in English] I will give you
what you want!

157
00:07:31,993 --> 00:07:33,244
[in English] I will tell you

158
00:07:33,327 --> 00:07:35,329
- where the laptop is!
- [Lily gasps]

159
00:07:35,413 --> 00:07:37,206
[Viktor, in English] Samir, that's enough.

160
00:07:37,290 --> 00:07:39,208
[in English] We need him alive.

161
00:07:40,084 --> 00:07:43,504
[in English] He is a professional.

162
00:07:45,256 --> 00:07:48,384
[in English] Military or police.

163
00:07:49,927 --> 00:07:54,015
[in English] I'm sure
he's trained to take any pain.

164
00:07:54,807 --> 00:07:56,142
[in English] No matter what we do,

165
00:07:56,225 --> 00:07:57,977
no matter what torture,

166
00:07:58,644 --> 00:08:00,605
he will not talk.

167
00:08:01,355 --> 00:08:03,774
[in English] And what will we do with him?

168
00:08:04,650 --> 00:08:08,237
[in English] His people
will be looking for him.

169
00:08:08,321 --> 00:08:11,073
[in English] We need
to take them both out!

170
00:08:11,157 --> 00:08:13,284
[in English] But ultimately,

171
00:08:14,076 --> 00:08:17,413
we have to get him to talk!

172
00:08:17,997 --> 00:08:20,750
[music swells]

173
00:08:28,508 --> 00:08:31,010
[in English] Wait a minute, huh.
Wait a minute, wait a minute.

174
00:08:31,636 --> 00:08:35,181
[in English] If Atoy is the father, hmm…

175
00:08:36,224 --> 00:08:37,517
who is the mother?

176
00:08:38,017 --> 00:08:39,685
I don't know.

177
00:08:39,769 --> 00:08:40,770
[pensive music playing]

178
00:08:40,853 --> 00:08:44,106
Atoy dated some women before,

179
00:08:44,190 --> 00:08:45,566
but nothing serious.

180
00:08:46,108 --> 00:08:49,779
From what I know, the only one
who really mattered to him was Audrey.

181
00:08:49,862 --> 00:08:53,282
And Audrey already had
a child with Atoy, Janine.

182
00:08:54,158 --> 00:08:56,702
OMG, Miss C!

183
00:08:56,786 --> 00:08:58,204
[suspicious music playing]

184
00:08:58,287 --> 00:09:02,208
Aren't Ibyang and Janine the same age?

185
00:09:02,291 --> 00:09:03,834
[Cita] Oh?

186
00:09:03,918 --> 00:09:06,754
Oh, then maybe Ibyang
is also Audrey's daughter.

187
00:09:06,837 --> 00:09:08,172
Maybe they were fraternal twins before,

188
00:09:08,256 --> 00:09:09,590
just separated by circumstances.

189
00:09:09,674 --> 00:09:14,262
You, Emerson, you've been watching
too many TV series reruns!

190
00:09:14,345 --> 00:09:18,182
Audrey and Atoy never said
their child had a twin, right?!

191
00:09:18,766 --> 00:09:20,268
I don't know about you!

192
00:09:20,351 --> 00:09:23,354
- Fraternal, because…
- Mmm, because--

193
00:09:23,437 --> 00:09:27,608
And Madam Martina also never mentioned
that Ibyang had a twin.

194
00:09:29,569 --> 00:09:30,861
[sighs]

195
00:09:33,155 --> 00:09:35,783
What if Audrey doesn't know this?

196
00:09:35,866 --> 00:09:37,034
Oh no.

197
00:09:37,118 --> 00:09:39,287
Audrey needs to know this.

198
00:09:39,370 --> 00:09:40,246
She's here.

199
00:09:40,329 --> 00:09:42,790
[music swells]

200
00:09:45,835 --> 00:09:47,044
Atoy.

201
00:09:47,128 --> 00:09:48,963
[music fades]

202
00:09:54,260 --> 00:09:56,012
- [Atoy] Lily.
- [Lily] Atoy.

203
00:09:56,095 --> 00:09:57,722
[Atoy] Take it, take it.

204
00:09:57,805 --> 00:09:58,764
Where did you get--

205
00:09:58,848 --> 00:09:59,932
Take it.

206
00:10:00,016 --> 00:10:02,560
- [tense music playing]
- [Lily straining]

207
00:10:02,643 --> 00:10:03,769
[Atoy] Open it.

208
00:10:03,853 --> 00:10:05,271
[Lily strains]

209
00:10:05,354 --> 00:10:06,606
Open it.

210
00:10:06,689 --> 00:10:07,690
[Lily] Wait.

211
00:10:07,773 --> 00:10:08,858
[Atoy] Did you get it?

212
00:10:08,941 --> 00:10:09,859
[Lily strains]

213
00:10:09,942 --> 00:10:10,943
That, that.

214
00:10:11,027 --> 00:10:12,903
[panting]

215
00:10:18,284 --> 00:10:19,243
Open it.

216
00:10:19,327 --> 00:10:20,411
Wait.

217
00:10:20,494 --> 00:10:21,829
[heavy breathing]

218
00:10:21,912 --> 00:10:23,581
Wait, it's locked.

219
00:10:23,664 --> 00:10:26,083
I've hacked complicated
computer systems before.

220
00:10:26,167 --> 00:10:28,127
What's a cell phone password anyway?

221
00:10:44,769 --> 00:10:49,607
Sister Ame told me why you're here now.

222
00:10:50,691 --> 00:10:52,193
Maybe…

223
00:10:52,276 --> 00:10:54,445
[sentimental music playing]

224
00:10:54,528 --> 00:10:58,157
…we should practice how to fight.

225
00:10:58,240 --> 00:10:59,075
Mmm.

226
00:11:00,868 --> 00:11:02,161
I have an idea!

227
00:11:02,244 --> 00:11:04,121
When Tatoy comes back,

228
00:11:04,205 --> 00:11:08,334
let's ask him to teach us
how to fight, so…

229
00:11:09,210 --> 00:11:12,713
we can defend ourselves.

230
00:11:14,048 --> 00:11:15,758
So, what? You in?

231
00:11:19,804 --> 00:11:22,681
We'll deal with the bad people.

232
00:11:23,265 --> 00:11:24,266
[music fades]

233
00:11:24,350 --> 00:11:29,814
- [imitating fighting sounds]
- [light music playing]

234
00:11:32,650 --> 00:11:34,485
You're funny too, huh?

235
00:11:35,319 --> 00:11:38,697
But are you sure you can fight?

236
00:11:39,532 --> 00:11:40,908
Of course.

237
00:11:42,034 --> 00:11:43,452
Once I learn,

238
00:11:44,161 --> 00:11:46,247
I'll defend Mama

239
00:11:46,330 --> 00:11:47,665
from those

240
00:11:48,374 --> 00:11:49,750
who are chasing her.

241
00:11:50,626 --> 00:11:53,295
Mama? You have a mama now?

242
00:11:53,379 --> 00:11:54,380
Where?

243
00:11:54,463 --> 00:11:55,297
[music fades]

244
00:11:55,381 --> 00:11:57,299
[Janine] Ah! I know.

245
00:11:57,383 --> 00:11:59,885
In your imagination?

246
00:12:01,137 --> 00:12:05,057
No, a real mama!

247
00:12:05,141 --> 00:12:06,934
She found me. Mmm.

248
00:12:07,017 --> 00:12:08,644
Now we're the same.

249
00:12:08,727 --> 00:12:10,104
[pensive music playing]

250
00:12:10,187 --> 00:12:12,148
Okay, now we're the same.

251
00:12:12,898 --> 00:12:14,608
Daddy. You have one too?

252
00:12:17,278 --> 00:12:19,280
Uh, well…

253
00:12:19,363 --> 00:12:20,990
Tatoy.

254
00:12:21,866 --> 00:12:23,951
Here we go again.

255
00:12:24,034 --> 00:12:26,912
Your real father, your blood relative!

256
00:12:28,330 --> 00:12:30,291
[music fades]

257
00:12:30,374 --> 00:12:31,584
[sniffles, then gasps]

258
00:12:31,667 --> 00:12:33,085
- There. There, it's done.
- [tense music playing]

259
00:12:33,586 --> 00:12:34,920
Ready?

260
00:12:35,004 --> 00:12:36,255
Okay, fine.

261
00:12:36,338 --> 00:12:37,798
Dial it.

262
00:12:37,882 --> 00:12:42,136
- [in English] 0-9-0…
- [Lily mumbles]

263
00:12:42,219 --> 00:12:43,721
- 7…
- Hm-mm.

264
00:12:43,804 --> 00:12:50,060
- 6-4-3-2-2-1.
- Uh-huh.

265
00:12:50,144 --> 00:12:51,479
[Lily] There.

266
00:12:54,899 --> 00:12:57,359
[phone ringing]

267
00:12:57,443 --> 00:12:59,445
[music swells]

268
00:13:05,493 --> 00:13:06,660
Hello?

269
00:13:07,786 --> 00:13:09,830
Ibyang. Ibyang!

270
00:13:09,914 --> 00:13:11,165
Ibyang, this is Atoy.

271
00:13:11,248 --> 00:13:12,458
Tatoy?!

272
00:13:12,541 --> 00:13:13,584
[intense music playing]

273
00:13:13,667 --> 00:13:16,128
Ibyang, Ibyang, I need your help.

274
00:13:16,212 --> 00:13:18,464
I--I--I was captured.

275
00:13:18,547 --> 00:13:21,091
I'm here in a car junkyard

276
00:13:21,175 --> 00:13:23,135
in… in San Rodolfo, Bulacan.

277
00:13:23,219 --> 00:13:25,054
San Rodolfo, hurry.

278
00:13:25,137 --> 00:13:25,971
Write it down.

279
00:13:26,055 --> 00:13:29,099
The owner is Viktor Petrov.

280
00:13:29,183 --> 00:13:30,726
[tense music playing]

281
00:13:30,809 --> 00:13:33,437
He's-- He's the ambassador
of the Zahran Embassy.

282
00:13:33,521 --> 00:13:35,439
Call my boss, Mercado.

283
00:13:35,523 --> 00:13:37,650
Call him. Tell him where I am.

284
00:13:37,733 --> 00:13:40,277
Y-Yes, yes, yes.

285
00:13:40,361 --> 00:13:44,907
Uh, car junkyard, San Rodolfo, Bulacan,

286
00:13:44,990 --> 00:13:46,700
owned by Viktor Petrov.

287
00:13:46,784 --> 00:13:48,327
Find Boss Mercado.

288
00:13:48,410 --> 00:13:49,328
[Atoy] <i>Okay, thank you.</i>

289
00:13:49,411 --> 00:13:51,830
Ibyang, Ibyang, don't--
don't ever call this number again.

290
00:13:51,914 --> 00:13:52,873
Did you hear me?

291
00:13:52,957 --> 00:13:54,708
Do you understand, huh?

292
00:13:54,792 --> 00:13:57,044
Okay, Tatoy.

293
00:13:57,127 --> 00:13:57,962
[keys drop and jingle]

294
00:13:58,045 --> 00:13:59,338
Call Mercado. Call--

295
00:13:59,421 --> 00:14:01,465
[tense music playing]

296
00:14:02,132 --> 00:14:03,050
[in English] What are you doing?

297
00:14:03,133 --> 00:14:04,593
[in English] Who are you talking to?

298
00:14:05,719 --> 00:14:06,762
But--

299
00:14:06,845 --> 00:14:08,138
That was Daddy, right?

300
00:14:08,681 --> 00:14:09,974
I want to talk to him.

301
00:14:10,057 --> 00:14:11,267
Call him again!

302
00:14:11,350 --> 00:14:12,309
He said it's prohibited!

303
00:14:12,393 --> 00:14:13,394
What do you mean prohibited?!

304
00:14:13,477 --> 00:14:15,646
- Oh, it's prohibited. Prohibited.
- But you talked to him yourself!

305
00:14:15,729 --> 00:14:16,897
He said it's not allowed.

306
00:14:16,981 --> 00:14:18,941
- That's unfair, Ibyang!
- Janine, please. Janine--

307
00:14:19,024 --> 00:14:20,651
- No-- Don't, Janine--
- Ibyang!

308
00:14:20,734 --> 00:14:21,902
[grunts]

309
00:14:21,986 --> 00:14:23,237
- [vendor] Thank you, miss.
- [Karla] Thank you.

310
00:14:26,365 --> 00:14:27,533
Karla.

311
00:14:27,616 --> 00:14:28,701
- Hi.
- Gavin!

312
00:14:31,161 --> 00:14:34,164
I gotta go now.
Our breakfast will get cold. All right.

313
00:14:34,248 --> 00:14:35,541
Breakfast with Uno?

314
00:14:36,333 --> 00:14:37,960
Why did he get involved?

315
00:14:38,627 --> 00:14:41,547
[in English] I don't know. Maybe
you're having breakfast together.

316
00:14:41,630 --> 00:14:43,132
Looks like you're really close to him.

317
00:14:44,049 --> 00:14:45,718
Who is that Uno really?

318
00:14:45,801 --> 00:14:47,261
[in English] Where did he come from?
What is he doing here?

319
00:14:47,344 --> 00:14:50,222
Uno and Atoy are workmates.

320
00:14:51,265 --> 00:14:53,726
- So is he also a tailor?
- [quirky music playing]

321
00:14:54,226 --> 00:14:55,561
New shop assistant?

322
00:14:56,186 --> 00:14:58,814
Why do you have
so many questios about him?

323
00:14:58,898 --> 00:15:01,358
It's because he is so arrogant,
acting like he is somebody big.

324
00:15:01,442 --> 00:15:03,611
And he's being way too familiar with you.

325
00:15:05,154 --> 00:15:06,655
So what?

326
00:15:06,739 --> 00:15:08,198
[quirky sting]

327
00:15:08,282 --> 00:15:14,121
Why don't you say all those
observations right to my face?

328
00:15:15,080 --> 00:15:17,625
That makes you look like
a total keyboard warrior.

329
00:15:17,708 --> 00:15:19,793
You're acting like a basher. Huh?

330
00:15:22,004 --> 00:15:23,088
[smirks]

331
00:15:23,672 --> 00:15:25,049
Do you know this woman?

332
00:15:25,633 --> 00:15:27,343
I'll ask my friend.

333
00:15:27,426 --> 00:15:29,178
[Uno] You're friend is really
something, huh?

334
00:15:29,261 --> 00:15:30,471
[Uno smirks]

335
00:15:31,639 --> 00:15:33,057
Hey!

336
00:15:33,140 --> 00:15:35,768
Bro, I will not hurt you.
Why are you hiding?

337
00:15:35,851 --> 00:15:37,603
What happened to your friend, Karla?

338
00:15:37,686 --> 00:15:38,646
[Karla] Gavin!

339
00:15:38,729 --> 00:15:40,064
Why are you hiding?

340
00:15:40,147 --> 00:15:42,399
Cha! Do you know her?

341
00:15:42,483 --> 00:15:44,109
[Cha] No.

342
00:15:44,193 --> 00:15:46,528
[tense music playing]

343
00:15:48,197 --> 00:15:49,239
[Uno] Hey!

344
00:15:50,157 --> 00:15:52,076
- Hey, are you okay?
- [in English] I have to warn Aunt Audrey.

345
00:15:52,159 --> 00:15:54,119
My dad's goon is here.

346
00:15:54,203 --> 00:15:55,579
Where?

347
00:16:03,087 --> 00:16:05,297
[in English] Nobody was talking. I--

348
00:16:05,881 --> 00:16:07,883
[in English] Liar. I heard a voice.

349
00:16:08,592 --> 00:16:10,344
[in English] He was-- [sniffles]
He was just…

350
00:16:10,928 --> 00:16:13,347
probably talking in his sleep, that's all.

351
00:16:14,390 --> 00:16:15,474
[groans]

352
00:16:15,557 --> 00:16:17,559
[sobs, in English] Please don't.
Please, just please stop.

353
00:16:17,643 --> 00:16:19,520
[pensive music playing]

354
00:16:19,603 --> 00:16:21,230
[Lily sobs]

355
00:16:24,650 --> 00:16:29,571
[in English] You know,
people call me many things.

356
00:16:30,864 --> 00:16:32,741
[in English] They call me a monster.

357
00:16:33,909 --> 00:16:36,495
[in English] Sometimes they say
I'm the devil.

358
00:16:38,622 --> 00:16:40,457
[in English] But you know,
they're all wrong.

359
00:16:40,541 --> 00:16:41,792
[tense music playing]

360
00:16:41,875 --> 00:16:43,127
[in English] You see,

361
00:16:43,877 --> 00:16:46,005
the devil brings temptation.

362
00:16:47,423 --> 00:16:49,008
[in English] I bring certainty.

363
00:16:50,384 --> 00:16:54,680
[in English] Tomorrow,
both of you will die.

364
00:16:55,556 --> 00:16:57,474
[music swells]

365
00:17:00,310 --> 00:17:04,481
[Lily sobbing]

366
00:17:08,652 --> 00:17:10,070
[music fades]

367
00:17:10,738 --> 00:17:14,992
[Lily sobbing]

368
00:17:17,953 --> 00:17:21,832
[Lily] Atoy, is this how
we're going to die?

369
00:17:23,459 --> 00:17:26,378
I didn't even get to see my child again.

370
00:17:26,462 --> 00:17:28,714
[pensive music playing]

371
00:17:32,843 --> 00:17:35,554
[sobbing]

372
00:17:35,637 --> 00:17:37,765
[Lily] Am I going to die here?

373
00:17:38,432 --> 00:17:40,142
[melodramatic music playing]

374
00:17:40,225 --> 00:17:42,186
That won't happen, Lily.

375
00:17:43,312 --> 00:17:44,563
[sobbing]

376
00:17:44,646 --> 00:17:46,899
Just trust, please.

377
00:17:48,233 --> 00:17:50,235
They will save us.

378
00:17:51,028 --> 00:17:52,738
[dramatic music playing]

379
00:18:16,887 --> 00:18:18,388
Do you know this man?

380
00:18:19,556 --> 00:18:20,974
Who is he?

381
00:18:21,058 --> 00:18:22,309
[man 1] No!

382
00:18:22,392 --> 00:18:23,310
- [henchman 1] Are you sure?
- [man 2] But

383
00:18:23,393 --> 00:18:25,604
he often hangs out
at the basketball court.

384
00:18:25,687 --> 00:18:27,022
Maybe he's there.

385
00:18:27,106 --> 00:18:28,273
- Thanks.
- Okay.

386
00:18:28,357 --> 00:18:29,566
- Let's go, bro.
- Let's go.

387
00:18:29,650 --> 00:18:33,403
[suspicious music playing]

388
00:18:33,487 --> 00:18:34,947
That's Gavin!

389
00:18:35,447 --> 00:18:36,949
You know, Audrey needs to know this.

390
00:18:37,032 --> 00:18:38,450
- I'll just call her. She's here--
- Wait, wait!

391
00:18:38,534 --> 00:18:39,660
[in English] Yes, my love?

392
00:18:41,245 --> 00:18:43,747
What if she's not the real mother?

393
00:18:43,831 --> 00:18:47,209
Right? Think about it. Atoy is handsome.

394
00:18:47,292 --> 00:18:51,964
It's not impossible that many women
wanted to get pregnant by him. Right?

395
00:18:52,047 --> 00:18:53,382
[Emerson] That's possible, possible.

396
00:18:53,465 --> 00:18:54,550
You have a point.

397
00:18:54,633 --> 00:18:57,261
You have a point, here.

398
00:18:57,344 --> 00:19:02,432
Well, actually, Atoy is really secretive
when it comes to women.

399
00:19:03,433 --> 00:19:05,686
So, only Atoy should know about this.

400
00:19:06,395 --> 00:19:11,316
Because only Atoy could possibly know
who Ibyang's real mother is.

401
00:19:12,109 --> 00:19:15,779
So, if possible,
while Atoy isn't here yet,

402
00:19:15,863 --> 00:19:18,240
no one should say anything to anyone.

403
00:19:18,323 --> 00:19:20,117
Even…

404
00:19:20,200 --> 00:19:22,661
Even about me being a fake mother.

405
00:19:22,744 --> 00:19:24,913
- [suspicious music playing]
- [heavy breathing]

406
00:19:26,623 --> 00:19:31,086
I want to be the one to tell
Atoy myself about his other child.

407
00:19:31,170 --> 00:19:32,462
Don't worry.

408
00:19:33,297 --> 00:19:37,092
We'll make sure no one finds out
about you being a fake mother,

409
00:19:37,176 --> 00:19:38,218
my love.

410
00:19:43,640 --> 00:19:46,018
[in English] Sorry, I overheard.

411
00:19:46,894 --> 00:19:48,812
[pensive music playing]

412
00:19:48,896 --> 00:19:51,231
Were you talking about

413
00:19:51,315 --> 00:19:52,900
Janine and Atoy?

414
00:19:54,401 --> 00:19:55,819
Uh, uh…

415
00:19:55,903 --> 00:19:59,031
Uh, I was just telling Olga that

416
00:19:59,114 --> 00:20:01,950
your and Janine's situation is dangerous.

417
00:20:02,034 --> 00:20:03,785
So, you should stay here while

418
00:20:03,869 --> 00:20:05,662
waiting for Atoy to return.

419
00:20:05,746 --> 00:20:07,539
You-- You're Olga?

420
00:20:10,042 --> 00:20:12,127
[Audrey] You're Ibyang's mother?

421
00:20:13,212 --> 00:20:14,504
Yes, I am.

422
00:20:15,214 --> 00:20:16,048
‪[Audrey sighs]

423
00:20:17,299 --> 00:20:18,133
‪[Olga sighs]

424
00:20:20,469 --> 00:20:21,845
Audrey, right?

425
00:20:22,638 --> 00:20:23,847
In fairness,

426
00:20:24,348 --> 00:20:26,892
Atoy really knows how to choose.

427
00:20:26,975 --> 00:20:28,185
You're beautiful, girl.

428
00:20:28,977 --> 00:20:30,312
[Audrey chuckles]

429
00:20:30,938 --> 00:20:31,980
[in English] Thank you.

430
00:20:32,064 --> 00:20:33,732
[gentle music playing]

431
00:20:34,316 --> 00:20:37,152
Uh, where is Ibyang?

432
00:20:37,986 --> 00:20:39,738
She's in the room.

433
00:20:39,821 --> 00:20:43,242
Um, we're staying here too,
until Atoy comes back.

434
00:20:44,618 --> 00:20:46,787
Not that you asked,

435
00:20:46,870 --> 00:20:49,498
but I also had a slight past with Atoy.

436
00:20:50,749 --> 00:20:54,795
- Um, we were supposed to date before.
- [whimsical music playing]

437
00:20:54,878 --> 00:20:57,297
But it didn't happen.

438
00:20:58,257 --> 00:20:59,800
Ah, really?

439
00:21:00,509 --> 00:21:03,011
[sighs, in English] What a small world.

440
00:21:03,762 --> 00:21:05,305
Can you believe it?

441
00:21:06,056 --> 00:21:07,808
You're Ibyang's mother.

442
00:21:07,891 --> 00:21:09,351
[sneaky music playing]

443
00:21:09,434 --> 00:21:11,186
[in English] It's a small world after all.

444
00:21:16,358 --> 00:21:17,859
Junkyard of cars.

445
00:21:17,943 --> 00:21:19,987
San Rodolfo, Bulacan.

446
00:21:20,487 --> 00:21:21,863
There's Viktor Petrov.

447
00:21:21,947 --> 00:21:23,657
- Ibyang? Uh…
- San Rodolfo, Bulacan.

448
00:21:24,324 --> 00:21:26,159
Are you hungry or possessed?

449
00:21:26,243 --> 00:21:27,619
You're saying so much.

450
00:21:27,703 --> 00:21:30,330
I should not forget it.

451
00:21:30,414 --> 00:21:31,915
Tatoy called.

452
00:21:31,999 --> 00:21:33,959
I spoke to him!

453
00:21:34,042 --> 00:21:35,627
My God! Thank God!

454
00:21:35,711 --> 00:21:37,379
Atoy is alive?

455
00:21:37,462 --> 00:21:39,464
Ibyang, what else did he say, huh?

456
00:21:39,548 --> 00:21:41,383
And where is he? Is he okay?

457
00:21:41,466 --> 00:21:43,635
What else? What else did he say?

458
00:21:43,719 --> 00:21:48,890
He said he needs help
because he was captured.

459
00:21:48,974 --> 00:21:49,933
[gasps]

460
00:21:50,017 --> 00:21:52,019
He said he's at--

461
00:21:52,102 --> 00:21:54,396
[suspicious music playing]

462
00:21:54,479 --> 00:21:57,649
At the car junkyard at…

463
00:21:58,275 --> 00:22:01,445
San Viktor-- I mean!

464
00:22:01,528 --> 00:22:02,863
San Rodolfo!

465
00:22:03,947 --> 00:22:05,449
In Bulacan.

466
00:22:06,783 --> 00:22:09,619
With Viktor Petrov.

467
00:22:09,703 --> 00:22:10,537
[music fades]

468
00:22:10,620 --> 00:22:13,040
V-Viktor Petrov?

469
00:22:13,123 --> 00:22:15,667
[tense music playing]

470
00:22:16,293 --> 00:22:18,962
So, he's being held
by the ambassador of Zahran!

471
00:22:19,588 --> 00:22:21,089
Is that what he told you?

472
00:22:22,174 --> 00:22:24,217
He didn't say that

473
00:22:24,301 --> 00:22:26,678
he was the one who captured him.

474
00:22:27,262 --> 00:22:28,638
Let's call the police!

475
00:22:29,264 --> 00:22:30,474
[Emerson] No, uh…

476
00:22:31,058 --> 00:22:33,268
The police can't just get in there easily.

477
00:22:33,351 --> 00:22:34,895
There are a lot of procedures
to go follow.

478
00:22:36,271 --> 00:22:39,107
He said we should find his boss,

479
00:22:39,191 --> 00:22:41,193
Mercado!

480
00:22:41,735 --> 00:22:42,819
[Olga] Mercado?

481
00:22:43,695 --> 00:22:45,447
[in English] As in Jennylyn Mercado?

482
00:22:45,530 --> 00:22:47,115
Ah-- What's that?

483
00:22:47,199 --> 00:22:48,950
He has a celebrity boss? Why?

484
00:22:49,034 --> 00:22:51,203
- I'm confused.
- No, uh…

485
00:22:51,286 --> 00:22:53,580
His boss is tougher than the police.

486
00:22:54,081 --> 00:22:56,708
We need to talk to Uno.
He's Mercado's man.

487
00:22:56,792 --> 00:22:58,376
[in English] Auntie, we have to go.

488
00:22:58,460 --> 00:23:00,378
I saw Daddy's men.

489
00:23:00,462 --> 00:23:01,755
They're looking for us.

490
00:23:01,838 --> 00:23:03,340
[in English] W-We can't leave.

491
00:23:03,423 --> 00:23:05,717
[stammers] What if Atoy comes back here?

492
00:23:05,801 --> 00:23:07,803
He won't find anyone.

493
00:23:08,887 --> 00:23:10,972
Uh, just stay here.

494
00:23:11,056 --> 00:23:13,809
No one from here will point you out.

495
00:23:13,892 --> 00:23:16,436
Gavin, do you know what they look like?

496
00:23:16,520 --> 00:23:18,438
My friend is the new town captain.

497
00:23:18,522 --> 00:23:20,524
I'll tell her to drive them away.

498
00:23:20,607 --> 00:23:22,859
[rousing music playing]

499
00:23:26,780 --> 00:23:30,826
[electronic blipping]

500
00:23:30,909 --> 00:23:32,702
[intense music playing]

501
00:23:36,331 --> 00:23:39,751
Miss, what did they say?
Will they save Atoy?

502
00:23:39,835 --> 00:23:42,170
Yes. He's talking to his boss inside.

503
00:23:42,254 --> 00:23:44,589
They said they'll send an extraction team.

504
00:23:44,673 --> 00:23:49,136
You know, if Uno is bringing anyone
to their operation, it should be me.

505
00:23:49,761 --> 00:23:52,556
Oh, oops! It fell.

506
00:23:52,639 --> 00:23:53,557
UP NEXT

507
00:23:53,640 --> 00:23:55,267
- You're peeking, bro.
- [gasps]

508
00:23:55,350 --> 00:23:56,810
[grunts]

509
00:23:56,893 --> 00:23:59,604
[Mongki] Our boys said Atoy is missing.

510
00:23:59,688 --> 00:24:01,731
I wish we were the ones who kidnapped him.

511
00:24:01,815 --> 00:24:03,066
But whoever did it, I hope…

512
00:24:03,150 --> 00:24:04,526
I hope they kill Atoy.

513
00:24:04,609 --> 00:24:05,861
[Lily] Where are you taking us?

514
00:24:05,944 --> 00:24:08,780
[in English] Didn't I tell you that today
is the day you'll die?

515
00:24:08,864 --> 00:24:10,407
[in English] And I'm a man of my word!

516
00:24:10,490 --> 00:24:12,159
[in English] So, prepare to die. Let's go!

517
00:24:12,242 --> 00:24:13,076
[in English] What are we waiting for?

518
00:24:13,160 --> 00:24:14,578
- [Lily] Atoy, what now, Atoy?
- [in English] Bring them! Let's go.

